WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.000
-Hi. I'm Jimmy Fallon
and welcome

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.200
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.067
It's Freaky Friday tonight.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:08.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.200
Hey, did you hear the big news
about Mike Pence?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.701
You remember him, right,

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.667
Casper the Homophobic Ghost?

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:17.200
[ Laughter ]
Mike Pence released
a policy agenda,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.501
which is a strong indication

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:21.400
that he plans to run
against Donald Trump in 2024.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.901
Pence versus Trump.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:23.968
Wouldn't that be something?

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.434
Like Logan Roy
versus Cousin Greg.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:29.167
[ Laughter ]
Meanwhile, Fox News
just announced

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:30.534
they've hired Caitlyn Jenner

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.667
as an on-air contributor
to their channel.

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.801
Fox put out a press release
that said,

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.300
"Caitlyn's story
is an inspiration to us all.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.501
She's a trailblazer
in the LGBTQ+ community

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:43.300
who will not be allowed to use
the bathroom at our office."

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:45.968
You know, I love being here
in New York

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:48.167
and I want to tell you
about this crazy thing

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.868
that happened in L.A. last week.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:52.067
So, you know the actor
Will Smith?

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:55.567
Oh, you've heard this story?
Okay. I didn't know

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:57.501
if it made it east,
so, I'll skip it, then.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:58.968
[ Laughter ]
Are you figuring out

00:00:58.968 --> 00:00:59.834
what's happening now?

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:01.901
You're noticing what day it is?

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:02.968
Or no. Maybe. I don't know.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.100
April Fools, everybody.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:12.100
Show of hands.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.467
How many of you
are disappointed?

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:14.267
Be honest.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.400
Okay, how many are very
disappointed? Be honest.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:22.968
And how many of you
are thinking,

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.067
"Oh, my God, Jimmy Fallon
looks terrible.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.033
I hope he isn't sick"?

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:27.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:28.834
We pulled the old switcheroo.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.901
In fact, right now,
Jimmy F-word,

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.200
as we call him back home,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.567
[ Laughter ]
is hosting my show in L.A.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.567
We swapped everything.

00:01:35.567 --> 00:01:37.534
We swapped shows, bands,

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:38.634
even wives.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:41.200
Bad news, Nancy --
Fat Jimmy's coming home.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.300
[ Laughter ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.701
This is something we've been
planning for a long --

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.567
for years.
It was a top secret operation.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.200
Even The Roots didn't know
this was happening

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.868
until today, right?
-No idea.

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.267
-Jimmy doesn't trust you,
is what --

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:54.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.167
Congratulations on that Oscar,
by the way.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.200
Questlove won an Oscar.
-Thank you.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.968
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:59.968 --> 00:02:01.901
-Nobody in my band has an Oscar.

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:04.067
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.634
-Not yet.
-And I have to say,

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:08.601
your movie is fantastic
and your speech was beautiful.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:12.400
Actually, I watched it as soon
as I stop rewinding 500 times.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.334
[ Laughter ]
Congratulations.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.701
Everybody here has been so nice.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.701
I got to meet Jimmy's writers.
I got to meet his producers.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.601
His security guy
took me on a tour.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.300
I even got to meet the chef

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.467
who cuts his chicken nuggets
into dinosaur shapes.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.634
[ Laughter ]
Wonderful guy.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.601
It's exciting to be here.

00:02:29.601 --> 00:02:32.334
This is really
I always dreamed of hosting

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:35.000
a late night talk show
and now, that dream

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.634
[ Laughter ]
has finally come true.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:37.734
Should we check in on Jimmy

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:39.400
to see how it's going
in Hollywood?

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.000
-Yeah!
-Yeah?

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.234
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.067
It was a rhetorical question,
really.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:47.701
You don't have a choice.
I'm checking in with Jimmy,

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:50.133
either way, but -- Oh, hey,
there's Jimmy right now.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
-And see how he's doing.
Jimmy, are you there?

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:53.834
-I'm here.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:54.934
I'm in your place.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:55.901
[ Whistling ]

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.400
-Yo!

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.434
[ Laughs ]
-Is this weird?

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:02.067
We did it!

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.000
Wow!
-Jimmy.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.634
A big chunk of your audience
almost left when I walked out.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.467
I saw sadness.
-Yeah, for the first time,

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:13.300
tonight I got a great
sitting ovation.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.400
[ Laughter ]
It was unbelievable.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.267
How's it going over there, bud?
You look great.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.267
-It's going well.
Everybody's been great

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:22.400
and I went through your stuff
and everything,

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.868
so, thank you
for letting me do this.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.467
We've been talking about this
for a long time,

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:29.033
I was just telling everybody.
-Right? April 2020.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:32.133
-April 2020
is when we conceived this.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.167
[ Laughter ]
-That's wild.

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.934
And do you like the studio?

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:35.767
Do you enjoy it?

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.367
-Not really, no.

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:38.567
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, no, yeah, it's beautiful.

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:39.734
It's absolutely beautiful.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.300
It makes me realize
what a dump our place is.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.968
[ Laughter ]
How about Guillermo,
is he alright?

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:46.601
Is he doing okay?

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.100
-Guillermo's okay.
C'mere, c'mere. C'mere, bud.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.834
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah, I have Guillermo.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:51.601
He's doing alright.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:52.934
He's okay.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.667
Guillermo.
-Hi, Jimmy!

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.534
-You look good.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.634
-Yeah, he's okay.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:01.734
-Guillermo, did you remember
to take your vitamins?

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:04.167
-Yeah, I did.
Took my vitamin tequila.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:06.467
-Okay, good.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:07.634
-He did, yeah.

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.200
Is Higgins there as well?

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.167
-Yeah, Higgins is right here
also, actually. He's --

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.567
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.167
He's freaky.
-I put on a mustache

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:16.634
so you'd feel at home, you know.
-Thank you!

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:17.934
-Grew a mustache.
-That's nice.

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:19.067
It's a great look for you.

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:20.667
-Good to see you, Higgins.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:23.434
-Higgins looks like
he should be swindling widows

00:04:23.434 --> 00:04:24.634
out of their fortune.

00:04:24.634 --> 00:04:25.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:28.701
-Flimflam, I say!

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.300
-Guillermo,
I'll be home tomorrow.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.968
If you need anything
before that, call Ellen, okay?

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:35.434
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Alright. I will, for sure.

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.000
-I don't know --
-This is wild, bud.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.434
It's been an amazing experience.

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.100
I love that we did this.
I can't believe

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.767
we pulled it off.
I really can't believe it.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:46.334
We did it. We pulled it off.
-I'm still not sure of how both

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:49.000
of our musical guests
are Red Hot Chili Peppers,

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.801
but I guess we'll figure
that out at the end of the show.

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:52.801
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Yeah. Yeah, that's right.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:55.567
Red Hot Chili Peppers are both
of our musical guests tonight.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:57.567
Their new album is out now,
at this point.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:05:00.334
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Alright, have fun.

00:05:00.334 --> 00:05:03.501
-Jimmy, this is magical.
I love it.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.667
I love talking to you, bud.
-Yeah, this is a lot of fun.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:08.067
And I especially love talking
to you over a satellite.

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:09.534
It's even better that way.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:11.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:14.100
-I agree. Alright, well,
I think we we should move on

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.734
with the show, alright?
What do you think?
-Yes. Okay.

00:05:15.734 --> 00:05:16.734
[ Cheering and applause ]
Yeah, great.

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:18.167
-Let's move on, yeah.

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:23.200
-Alright.
You want to hang up?

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.701
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:27.167
You hang up first.
-No, you hang up.
Come on, you hang up.

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:29.534
[ Laughter ]
-No, you hang up first.
-No, you hang up!

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:30.868
-No, you hang up.
No, you hang up.

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:32.834
No, you hang up.
-We'll hang up at the same time,
alright?

00:05:32.834 --> 00:05:35.400
Ready?
1, 2, 3.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.934
-2.
-Oh, well, we got it
all screwed up.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.300
[ Laughter ]
Alright.
-Oh, he did hang up.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.167
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:42.367
-I'll see you at home, Jimmy.

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:44.200
Alright, well,
that's Jimmy Fallon in L.A.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.267
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:48.467
It's going to be fun.
Don't be bummed.

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:49.734
Bridget Everett is with us.

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:51.901
We have music from
Red Hot Chili Peppers tonight.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:56.133
And, from "The Music Man,"
the toast of Broadway,

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:58.934
Hugh Jackman, Wolverine himself,
is here with us.

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:00.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.133
Or maybe it'll turn out to be
Hugh Grant.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:03.968
Who knows?
Anything is possible tonight.

